  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COVID-19 Vaccine procurement for Polynesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Activity is supporting Polynesian countries (the Cook Islands, Niue, Samoa, Tokelau, Tonga, and Tuvalu) to achieve high levels of COVID-19 vaccination coverage and reduce the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic through the provision of COVID-19 vaccines from New Zealand&apos;s domestic stocks. It reimburses the Ministry of Health and Pharmac (from April 2023) for the cost of vaccines procured.</narrative>
  </description>
